    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45 degrees incidence. Initialize with quarter-wave ratio scaffold where t_TiO2/t_SiO2 = 0.60 anchored to the best-performing candidate thicknesses from prior iteration (Layer 2 SiO2 thickness as reference). Apply differential evolution optimizer with population size 40, mutation factor F=0.9, crossover rate CR=0.85. Enforce strict layer-count locking to prevent topology changes during mutation. Evaluate reflectance in 450-650 nm band and transmittance in 700-1000 nm band. Include ±5 nm absolute thickness tolerance for robustness scoring. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
